    "keep_threshold_deg": 15.0,
    "model": "a dielectric mirror (IOR 1.376) at the measured corneal position, rendered with the plate camera, masked to the corneal cap, reduced to its compact part and added",
    "compact_only": "the render minus its own local baseline. separate_specular.py only removes what stands above the local diffuse level, so the broad dim corneal reflection of the original room is STILL IN D. Adding the full mirror wash on top double-counts it and reads as a contact lens over the whole iris",
    "why_not_painted": "presence, size, shape, colour and occlusion all come from the scene. A distance rule would get sunlight backwards: a mirror shows RADIANCE, which does not fall off with distance, so the sun makes a tiny brilliant spark rather than nothing",
    "keep_or_replace": "computed from two MEASURED angles -- the plate key from its own catchlights, the scene key from the L1 moment of the rendered irradiance. Not an artist setting"
